===Etymology===
From {{etyl|VL.|it}} {{m|la|ceresia}}, from the neuter plural of {{etyl|LL.|it}} {{m|la|ceresium}}, from {{etyl|la|it}} {{m|la|cerasium}}, from {{etyl|grc|it}} {{m|grc|κεράσιον||cherry|sc=polytonic}}, from {{etyl|grc|it}} {{m|el|κερασός||[[bird cherry]]}}, ultimately possibly of {{etyl|ine-ana|it}} origin. Alternatively from ''[[ciliegio]]'', ''[[ciriegio]]'' (Tuscan), from {{etyl|LL.|it}} ''ceresus'', from {{etyl|la|it}} {{m|la|cerasus}}. See also {{m|it|cerasa}}.

